          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 36,
              "body": "This could be read as cheerleading rather than a description of technical capabilities.  \"advanced\" \"surgical\".\n\nI'm not saying you're wrong.  But if the spec comes off as a marketing piece to someone when they first read it, they'll be turned off and stay that way.",
              "createdAt": "2026-02-28T05:29:55Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-02-28T05:29:55Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOQZxkd87mrSN2",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "3c08638"
          },
          "author": "selfissued",
          "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
          "state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
          "body": "This is too long and restates some things we've already stated.  It should be more concise and come off as declarative rather than promotional.\n\nCan we make the same essential points with less than half the words?",
          "createdAt": "2026-02-28T05:31:48Z",
