          "author": "skyfire-ankit",
          "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "Hey @selfissued I have rewritten use-cases 3 and 4 to focus on KYAPay vs trying to explain what we saw missing in other protocols that led us to inventing something new. Please take a look. \ud83d\ude4f ",
          "createdAt": "2026-02-28T17:10:34Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-02-28T17:36:16Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 19,
              "body": "I will try to rewrite this but TBH the explanation seemed technical to me. In any case, let me give it another shot.",
              "createdAt": "2026-02-28T17:10:34Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-02-28T17:36:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 20,
              "body": "I will rewrite but I think this is important to call out so that each use-case can stand independently.",
              "createdAt": "2026-02-28T17:11:29Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-02-28T17:36:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 28,
              "body": "Makes sense. In both use-case 3 and 4, my intent was to clarify that we looked at mTLS and HTTP message signatures but they didn't meet the needs that we see and thats why we invented KYAPay. But I will rewrite and focus on why KYAPay works so that it does not sound negative to the other protocols.",
              "createdAt": "2026-02-28T17:18:14Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-02-28T17:36:16Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 36,
              "body": "Makes sense. I will rewrite.",
              "createdAt": "2026-02-28T17:18:27Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-02-28T17:36:16Z"
            }
